;;;6176    *
;;;6177    * Aborts all active GAP procedures and prevents new ones from being started.
;;;6178    * This function is used to ensure an idle GAP so that the controller's
;;;6179    * resolving list can be modified.  When done accessing the resolving list, the
;;;6180    * caller must call `ble_gap_preempt_done()` to permit new GAP procedures.
;;;6181    *
;;;6182    * On preemption, all aborted GAP procedures are reported with a status or
;;;6183    * reason code of BLE_HS_EPREEMPTED.  An attempt to initiate a new GAP
;;;6184    * procedure during preemption fails with a return code of BLE_HS_EPREEMPTED.
